From: GT-BE19000AI kernel development
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] arm64: backport AArch32 time64 syscall ABI

Add Linux v5.1 ARM EABI time64 entry numbers without changing the old
vendor time32 ABI. Reuse native 64-bit time handlers only where the whole
argument layout matches. Preserve compat fd sets, signal masks, siginfo,
message headers and nested pointers for compound interfaces. The new AIO
signal descriptor explicitly uses a 32-bit pointer; CONFIG_AIO remains off.

Mask compat timespec nanosecond padding in get_timespec64 and make the
shared native futex handler use that helper. Do not alter task, scheduler,
network, block or vendor module-facing structure layouts.

ABI references: Linux v5.1; upstream y2038-new-syscalls tag
48166e6ea47d23984f0b481ca199250e1ce0730a. This is a scoped ARM64 compat
backport, not a wholesale rename of time32 functions or kernel upgrade.

